    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **Fixed governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was importing these as named exports from the module, but they were only available via the default export\n   - This fixed the \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'join')\" error in the governance tests\n\n### 2. **Fixed toxicity metric** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - Changed `toxicityMetric` function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs)`\n   - The issue was that `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but toxicity doesn't need references\n   - Previously, the references array was being incorrectly used as banned terms, causing valid outputs to be flagged\n   - Now it always uses the default banned terms\n\n## Test Results\n\n**Before:** 2 failed, 26 passed\n**After:** 28 passed \u2713\n\n### Commands run:\n```bash\npnpm --filter frai-core test    # All 28 tests passing\npnpm --filter frai-core build   # Build successful\n```",
